\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Fig. 6. Reconciliation time versus conflict-group size (log scale) on partial ballots. CF-RP is sub-millisecond for typical groups (M $\leq $ 20), 1.35 ms at M = 30, 4.4 ms at M = 50, and $\approx 21$ ms at M = 100—an extreme case; causal pre-locking adds no measurable overhead over plain Ranked Pairs. LWW and VC detection are cheaper but produce the quality losses measured above.}}{20}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:6}{{6}{20}{Fig. 6. Reconciliation time versus conflict-group size (log scale) on partial ballots. CF-RP is sub-millisecond for typical groups (M $\leq $ 20), 1.35 ms at M = 30, 4.4 ms at M = 50, and $\approx 21$ ms at M = 100—an extreme case; causal pre-locking adds no measurable overhead over plain Ranked Pairs. LWW and VC detection are cheaper but produce the quality losses measured above}{figure.6}{}}
